Predict strong negative values for 'because' and 'since', weaker negatives
for reason-word translations, 'although', 'due to', and 'even though'.
For 'that', check the preceding word for premise, purpose, notice, or
statement expressions. 'For' has a weak negative response, reduced after
some common preceding words. Case, spacing, and document starts adjust estimates.
Keep only the previous token's word; reset context at document boundaries.
Unrecognized tokens predict zero, leaving weak incidental responses unmodeled.
