"""Negative responses to the lexical family of PASS.

Bare 'pass' is strongest; inflections, passage, French 'pas', and related
Chinese words are weaker. Failure and passwords also trigger it. A split
word can trigger again on its ending (for example PAS + SED). Case and
whether punctuation is attached change the strength. Other tokens get zero.
These rules describe spelling and word classes, not success of an action.
"""
READS = ()

PAST_WORDS = {'过去', '過去', '经过', '經過', '过了', '过的'}
PASSING_WORDS = {'通过', '通過', '超过', '超過', '不过', '不過'}
ARRIVAL_OR_TRANSMISSION = {'通', '达', '達', '传', '傳', '渡', '达到'}


